Z||000000||coolcat||07-06-2001||03:13 AM||||I just purchased a 87 T-TOP and was wondering if there are differences between 87 and 88 T-TOPs,if so what are they.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headbang.gif"> Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||5
Z||000001||RossT||07-06-2001||03:27 AM||||cool cat, There are only slight differences in the weatherseals. Also keep in mind that several 88's were converted to t-tops after they were delivered to the dealer.  Thus you have 88's with the factory CJB code (t-top) and 88's without the factory code (like mine)<BR>Those without the code are the same as the 84-87's. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||07-06-2001||09:39 AM||||Besides the seals I think their may have been a slight difference on the external metal edge of the t-top. I have a new one on my car and the original in the garage. The original is just slightly different. <P>Thinking I have an 88 top as the replacement for my earlier top maybe. Anyone else noticed this?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||07-06-2001||09:54 AM||||I have also noticed that the 88 CJB cars have<BR>crome locks and the 84-88 non CJB cars have black lock cyclinder.<P>As far as the metal part being different, I am unsure.  Tim from <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A>  would know. Tims site indicates that replacement tops fit all cars (cjb and non) <BR>Also John P. might know. I can only guess as to why that is.<P>I also noticed that the t-tops straps that I have are slightly different than the 88 cjb cars.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||07-06-2001||11:55 AM||||all i know is...<P>i wish i had t-tops.<P>maybe on my next car.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIERO JOHN-WI||07-06-2001||03:28 PM||||Hi guys, the trim piece shouldn't be different at all but when you had 200 autherized dealer that could install the t-tops for  the fiero there will be differences and I have seen MANY!  Even all the literature I have for the pre factory ones do not show any part number change at all for that piece.  As for some of the difference I have seen(I saw only one thing that looked good, that they should have done with the factory ones)<BR>That is: Your t-top dome light cover that goes over the regular dome light, well if you look where the two meet in the center(where the lights are) around the edge the 2 plastics don't but up tight and if you try to tighten the screws tighter all you end up doing is dis-figuring it ! Well this one pre t-top car had a 1/16 or 1/8 didn't measure , piece of plastic cut a little bigger then the t-top dome plate , so when you have it basically sandwhiched between the factory dome light and the t-top housing it filled in the gap and gave a very finished off look (only down fall you have to unscrew the t-top dome light housing if you ever have to change a light bulb) But how offen do you replace them?||||reg||6
Z||000006||FIERO JOHN-WI||07-06-2001||04:15 PM||||That was the only thing good, but I've seen a lot of hack jobs and what's really scary sometimes from the same place! I guess it's really true when people say that must have been done on a Friday (quick and halfas* so they can get out of work) or monday (very tired and don't really don't care if something lines up) but then I've seen perfection as well from the same place. If I have time next week and were still talking about this subject i'll list some of the hack-up things i've seen and I'm sure Mr. fiero could also list some things he has seen .||||reg||1
